# Implementation Plan - Phase 5: Offline-First & Sync

This plan implements Phase 5 of the mobile PWA guide, focusing on ensuring the app remains functional without an internet connection and synchronizes data once reconnected.

## Proposed Changes

### [NEW] [SyncContext.jsx](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/frontend/src/context/SyncContext.jsx)
- Monitor `navigator.onLine` status.
- Manage a `syncQueue` in `localStorage`.
- Provide a `queueRequest` function to save failed mutations.
- Automatically attempt to sync the queue when the browser returns online.

### [NEW] [BudgetContext.jsx](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/frontend/src/context/BudgetContext.jsx)
- Centralize state for transactions, income, and goals.
- Persist state to `localStorage` for offline viewing.
- Support "Optimistic Updates" where local state is updated immediately with a `isPending` flag.

### [MODIFY] [api.js](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/frontend/src/api/api.js)
- Update mutation functions ([addTransaction](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/frontend/src/api/api.js#340-348), [updateTransaction](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/frontend/src/api/api.js#367-375), [deleteTransaction](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/frontend/src/api/api.js#376-383), etc.) to optionally bypass standard error handling if offline, allowing the caller to queue the request.

### [MODIFY] [App.jsx](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/frontend/src/App.jsx)
- Wrap the application in `SyncProvider` and `BudgetProvider`.

### [MODIFY] [TransactionsMobile.jsx](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/frontend/src/pages/mobile/TransactionsMobile.jsx)
- Switch from local `useState` for transactions to `useBudget`.
- Update [handleSubmit](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/frontend/src/pages/mobile/TransactionsMobile.jsx#196-223) to handle offline state by adding to the sync queue and updating UI optimistically.
- Display a "Pending" icon for transactions that haven't been synced yet.

### [MODIFY] [Navbar.jsx](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/frontend/src/components/mobile/Navbar.jsx)
- Add a subtle offline indicator (e.g., a "Cloud-Off" icon or color shift) when the device is offline.

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- I will search for a testing framework (e.g. Vitest/Jest). Since none were found, I'll recommend adding a basic test setup if out of scope, or verify via manual browser testing.

### Manual Verification
1. **Offline Mode Detection**:
   - Open the app in the browser.
   - Use DevTools "Network" tab to set mode to "Offline".
   - Verify `Navbar` shows the offline indicator.
2. **Offline Data Creation**:
   - In "Offline" mode, add a new transaction.
   - Verify the transaction appears in the list immediately with a "Pending" icon.
   - Refresh the page and verify the transaction is still there (persisted in `localStorage`).
3. **Synchronization**:
   - Switch back to "Online" mode.
   - Verify the "Pending" icon disappears after a few seconds.
   - Verify the transaction exists in the backend (check console logs or refresh again).
4. **Data Consistency**:
   - Ensure that fetching new data while online doesn't overwrite pending offline changes in an inconsistent way.
